From 3743d596e0cc4f3625f11c156f868bae03755d23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deep Audit <audit@cobuddy.local>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 11:48:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Deep i18n re-audit round 3: fix 4 genuinely hidden bugs

Full manual verification from fresh clone (latest commit 2defc7f), not
trusting any prior "Verified"/"Fixed" claims. Cross-checked all 96
useTranslation() namespaces against registration (96/96 match), all 92
locale JSON files against index.ts imports (no orphans), and manually
traced all 14 dynamic t(ns.${var}) call sites against every possible
value their variables can take.

Found 4 real bugs, all invisible when testing in English (fallback text
always matches the English literal, so only non-English locales break):

1. src/screens/safety/TrustedContactsScreen.tsx:197
   t(rel_${rel.toLowerCase()}, rel) was missing the 'contacts.' namespace
   prefix that every other t() call in this file uses. The key only exists
   nested under contacts.rel_family/rel_friend/etc, not at namespace root,
   so relationship chips (Family/Friend/Partner/Other) never translated.
   Fix: added 'contacts.' prefix.

2. src/services/mock/onboarding.mock.ts + onboarding/location.json
   Mock data references keys location.benefits.discovery.title and
   location.benefits.transit.title, but the JSON file had these stored
   under different key names: benefits.venue and benefits.routes.
   "Venue Discovery" and "Protected Routes" permission benefit cards never
   translated. Fix: renamed JSON keys venue->discovery, routes->transit
   to match the code's lookup keys.

3. src/services/mock/onboarding.mock.ts + onboarding/notification.json
   Same class of bug: code looks up notification.benefits.alerts.title
   but JSON had it stored as benefits.safety. "Safety Pings" benefit
   card never translated. Fix: renamed safety->alerts in JSON.

4. src/screens/bookings/DisputeRefundScreen.tsx:60,64
   'Companion: ' and 'Session Date: ' label prefixes were hardcoded raw
   JSX text, never wrapped in t() at all (only the fallback values next
   to them were translated). Fix: wrapped both labels in t(), added
   labelCompanion/labelSessionDate keys to bookings/dispute.json.

Verified via:
- Full namespace-registration cross-check (96/96 match)
- Orphan-file check (92/92 disk files imported, 0 orphans)
- All 14 dynamic t() call sites manually traced against every possible
  variable value (arrays, mock data, enums) - values vs JSON keys diffed
- npx tsc --noEmit: 0 errors
- python3 json.load() on all 92 locale files: 0 invalid

Not fixed / flagged as product judgment call (unchanged from prior audit):
CompanionProfileScreen hobbies/personality/rules, SavedProfilesScreen
tags, and review comments are freeform per-user/per-companion content,
not fixed app vocabulary - left untranslated pending product input.
Language picker screens (LanguageSelectionScreen, SpokenLanguagesScreen)
intentionally show language names in their native script/English name,
which is standard UX for language pickers, not a bug.
